### Login as A (reports items)
# @name loginA
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "test1234"
}

### Login as B (claimant)
# @name loginB
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "other@example.com",
  "password": "other1234"
}


### TEST 1: Without login (must be 401)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/me/items

### TEST 2: A's items
GET http://localhost:3000/api/me/items
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.token}}

### TEST 3: B's claims
GET http://localhost:3000/api/me/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.token}}

### TEST 4: Claims received by A
GET http://localhost:3000/api/me/received-claims
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.token}}

### TEST 5: Claims received by B
GET http://localhost:3000/api/me/received-claims
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.token}}